-- title:
--   Smooth-point stalks yield smooth-point packages at full level
-- statement:
--   The ambient frame is the following. A prime $q$ with $5 \le q$, a nonzero natural number $M'$ with $q \nmid M'$, and a valuation subring $A$ of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}} =$ `AlgebraicClosure ℚ` with `hA : A.LiesOverPrime q`, i.e. $q$ is a nonunit of $A$. A finite set $W$ of places of `modularFunctionFieldC (ResidueField A) M'` over the residue field of $A$, characterised by `hW` as consisting exactly of the members of `ssPlaces q M' (ResidueField A)`, that is of the places $w$ that are rational, satisfy the predicate `IsAffineGeomPlace` and whose value `w.evalAt (jGeomGen …)` lies in `ssJSet q`; together with a distinguished element $s$ of $W$. An inclusion `hle` of `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` (the $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$-base change `laurentBaseChange` of the full modular function field `modularFunctionFieldFull M'`) into `fieldBar q M'` (the $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$-base change of the function field of $X_H$ of level $q^2M'$ for $H =$ `levelH q M'`), both viewed inside the Laurent series field over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$. A constant reduction $R_0$ of $A$ from `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` to `modularFunctionFieldC (ResidueField A) M'`, that is: a valuation subring `R₀.integers`, a surjective residue homomorphism onto the special fibre field whose kernel is the maximal ideal, a map `placeMap` on places preserving degrees, the condition that a constant is integral exactly when it lies in $A$, compatibility of the residue with the residue of $A$ on constants, the normalisation `exists_smul_mem`, and the divisor-pushforward compatibility `mapDomain_placeMap`; and `hR₀`, which says that for every Laurent series $y$ with coefficients in $A$ whose image under coefficientwise inclusion lies in `modularFunctionFieldBar M'`, that image is $R_0$-integral and its $R_0$-residue, read as a Laurent series over `ResidueField A`, is the coefficientwise reduction of $y$.
--
--   Next, the small-constant frame: an intermediate field $k_0$ of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}/\mathbb{Q}$ and an element $\pi_0 \in k_0$ lying in $A$, such that $A \cap k_0$ (the comap of $A$ along $k_0 \to \overline{\mathbb{Q}}$) is a discrete valuation ring (`hdvr`) with maximal ideal generated by $\pi_0$ (`hunif`), is Henselian local (`hhens`) and has algebraically closed residue field (`hres`), together with `hκ`: every $a \in A$ differs from some $c \in k_0 \cap A$ by an element of the maximal ideal of $A$. Then auxiliary constants: a prime $\ell$ with $3 \le \ell$, $\ell \ne q$ and $\ell \nmid M'$; an element $\zeta_0 \in k_0$ which is a primitive $(q\ell)$-th root of unity in $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$; and an element $\varpi_t \in k_0$ lying in $A$ with $\varpi_t^{\,q^2-1} = q\,u$ for some unit $u$ of $A$. Finally the layer data: an index type $\iota$, a family $K : \iota \to$ intermediate fields of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}/k_0$ with each $K_n$ finite over $k_0$, and valuation subrings $A_n$ of $K_n$ with $x \in A_n \iff x \in A$ (so $A_n = A \cap K_n$).
--
--   With $k_0$ acting on `fieldBar q M'` through $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$, the assertion is universally quantified over: an intermediate field $F_0$ of `fieldBar q M'` over $k_0$ such that the $k_0$-subfield generated by the constants $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ together with $F_0$ is everything; a field $FSS$ with an algebra structure over `ResidueField A`; a regular prolongation $R$ of $A$ from `fieldBar q M'` to $FSS$ (a valuation subring `R.integers` of `fieldBar q M'` containing exactly those constants that lie in $A$, with a surjective residue map onto $FSS$ whose kernel is the maximal ideal, compatible with the residue of $A$ on constants, and satisfying `exists_smul_mem`); a finite set $N$ of places of $FSS$ over `ResidueField A`; subrings $S_n(Q)$ of `fieldBar q M'` indexed by places $Q$ of $FSS$ and layers $n$; ring homomorphisms $\varphi_n(Q) : A_n[X] \to S_n(Q)$; ring homomorphisms $\chi_n(Q) : S_n(Q) \to$ `ResidueField A`; and sets $D_n(Q)$ of places of `fieldBar q M'` over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$. Throughout, $F_n$ denotes the $k_0$-subfield `IntermediateField.adjoin k₀ (image of K n in fieldBar q M') ⊔ F₀`.
--
--   The hypothesis is the conjunction: $\#N = q+1$; for every place $Q \notin N$, first, for every layer $n$, the eighteen clauses — (i) the map $A_n \to$ `ResidueField A` induced by the residue of $A$ is surjective; (ii) the image in `fieldBar q M'` of every $a \in A_n$ lies in $S_n(Q)$; (iii) $\varphi_n(Q)$ is formally smooth and formally unramified; (iv) $\varphi_n(Q)(C\,a)$ is the image of $a$ in `fieldBar q M'`; (v) $\chi_n(Q)(\varphi_n(Q)(C\,a))$ is the residue of $a$; (vi) $\chi_n(Q)(\varphi_n(Q)(X)) = 0$; (vii) for every $c \in A_n$ with residue $0$ there is exactly one ring homomorphism $\chi : S_n(Q) \to A_n$ splitting the constants, compatible with $\chi_n(Q)$ after reduction, and sending $\varphi_n(Q)(X)$ to $c$; (viii) every $f \in S_n(Q)$ is $R$-integral, its $R$-residue lies in the valuation subring of $Q$, and the residue there is the image of $\chi_n(Q)(f)$ in the residue field of $Q$; (ix) $\varphi_n(Q)(X)$ is $R$-integral and the $Q$-order of its $R$-residue is $1$; (x) $P \in D_n(Q)$ holds exactly when $P$ is rational, every $f \in S_n(Q)$ lies in the valuation subring of $P$ with $P.\mathrm{evalAt}(f) \in A$, and $A$-valuation of $P.\mathrm{evalAt}(f)$ is $<1$ exactly when $\chi_n(Q)(f) = 0$; (xi) $\varphi_n(Q)(X) \ne \varphi_n(Q)(C\,c)$ for every $c \in A_n$; (xii) $S_n(Q)$ is local with maximal ideal the kernel of $\chi_n(Q)$, Noetherian, and a unique factorisation monoid; (xiii) $S_n(Q) \subseteq F_n$; (xiv) every element of $F_n$ is a quotient of two elements of $S_n(Q)$ with nonzero denominator; (xv) linear disjointness: if $c : \mathrm{Fin}\,m \to \overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ is linearly independent over $K_n$ and $a_i \in F_n$ satisfy $\sum_i c_i a_i = 0$, then all $a_i = 0$; (xvi) for every ring homomorphism $\chi : S_n(Q) \to A_n$ splitting the constants and compatible with $\chi_n(Q)$, the kernel of $\chi$ is generated by $\varphi_n(Q)(X) - \varphi_n(Q)(C(\chi(\varphi_n(Q)(X))))$; (xvii) there is a nonzero generator $\varpi$ of the maximal ideal of $A_n$ such that $\varphi_n(Q)(C\,\varpi)$ is prime in $S_n(Q)$, such that an element of $F_n$ is $R$-integral exactly when it is a quotient $g/h$ with $g,h \in S_n(Q)$ and $\varphi_n(Q)(C\,\varpi) \nmid h$, and such that for every prime $p$ of $S_n(Q)$ not associated to $\varphi_n(Q)(C\,\varpi)$ and every $x \in S_n(Q)$ there is a monic polynomial $r$ over $A_n$ with $p$ dividing the value at $x$ of $r$ pushed forward along $\varphi_n(Q) \circ C$; (xviii) finite generation: there is a finite subset $G$ of $S_n(Q)$ such that every $f \in S_n(Q)$ satisfies $f h = g$ with $g, h$ in the subring generated by $G$ together with the image of $A_n$, and $h$ the image of a unit of $S_n(Q)$. Second, the cross-layer clause: there is a monotonicity witness $S_n(Q) \le S_{n'}(Q)$ whenever $K_n \le K_{n'}$, such that $S_{n'}(Q)$ lies in the subring generated by $S_n(Q)$ together with the image of $A_{n'}$ whenever $K_n \le K_{n'}$, the coordinates $\varphi_n(Q)(X)$ agree in `fieldBar q M'` for all pairs of layers, and $\chi_{n'}(Q)$ restricts along the inclusion to $\chi_n(Q)$ whenever $K_n \le K_{n'}$. The hypothesis further contains: separation — if $Q, Q' \notin N$ and some $P$ lies in both $D_n(Q)$ and $D_n(Q')$, then $Q = Q'$; cusp-avoidance — for $Q \notin N$, every layer $n$ and every $P \in D_n(Q)$, the order at $P$ of the image in `fieldBar q M'` of the $q$-expansion `jq` (transported by `coeffEmb` into `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` and then along `hle`) is nonnegative; and equivariance — for every $\tau$ in the subgroup of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$-automorphisms of `fieldBar q M'` generated by the automorphisms `levelAutBar q M' ζ γ` with $\zeta$ a primitive $q$-th root of unity and $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$, and every proof that $\tau$ preserves `R.integers`, the induced residue automorphism `R.resAut τ` acts on places so that $\mathrm{resAut}(\tau)\cdot Q \in N \iff Q \in N$, and for $Q \notin N$ and every layer $n$, `smulDisc τ (Dn Q n)`, i.e. $\{P : \tau^{-1}\cdot P \in D_n(Q)\}$, equals $D_n(\mathrm{resAut}(\tau)\cdot Q)$.
--
--   The conclusion asserts, for the same five data $N, S_n, \varphi_n, \chi_n, D_n$: $\#N = q+1$; and for every $Q \notin N$, first, for every layer $n$, the clauses (i)–(x) above verbatim, followed by four further clauses — (xi$'$) for every ring homomorphism $\chi : S_n(Q) \to A_n$ splitting the constants and compatible with $\chi_n(Q)$ after reduction, there is exactly one place $P$ with $P \in D_n(Q)$ and $P.\mathrm{evalAt}(f) = \chi(f)$ for all $f \in S_n(Q)$; (xii$'$) for every $P \in D_n(Q)$ and every $f \in F_n$, $f$ lies in the valuation subring of $P$ exactly when $f h = g$ for some $g, h \in S_n(Q)$ with $P.\mathrm{evalAt}(h) \ne 0$; (xiii$'$) for every nonzero $f \in F_n$ whose order at every $P \in D_n(Q)$ vanishes, there are a nonzero $c \in K_n$ and a unit $u$ of $S_n(Q)$ with $c \cdot f = u$ in `fieldBar q M'`; (xiv$'$) every $f \in F_n$ that is $R$-integral and lies in the valuation subring of every $P \in D_n(Q)$ belongs to $S_n(Q)$ — and then clause (xviii) (finite generation) verbatim. Second, the same cross-layer clause with monotonicity witness, generation of $S_{n'}(Q)$, agreement of the coordinates and compatibility of the characters; and finally the same three clauses: separation of the places $Q \notin N$ by their discs, nonnegativity of the order of $j$ at every $P \in D_n(Q)$, and equivariance of $N$ and of the discs under the subgroup generated by the level automorphisms `levelAutBar q M' ζ γ`, $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$.
--
--   Thus the implication keeps the sections, residue-character, disc-description, $Q$-order and finite-generation clauses, adds the bijection between $A_n$-sections and points of the disc, the description of the local rings of points of the disc inside $F_n$, the unit principle and the characterisation of $S_n(Q)$ as the $R$-integral functions regular on $D_n(Q)$, while the structural clauses (xi)–(xvii) of the hypothesis are not repeated in the conclusion.
--
--   This is the passage from the layerwise smooth-point data of the supersingular model (local étale $A_n$-coordinate rings with residue characters and residue discs) to the full package in which residue discs correspond to $A_n$-valued sections, the local ring of each point of a disc is the expected localisation, the unit principle holds, and the coordinate ring is recovered as the $R$-integral functions regular on the disc; the upgrade is performed at fixed witnesses, using the generic statement [`AlgebraicCurve.RegularProlongation.disc_sections_locality_of_smoothPoint`](thm.html#AlgebraicCurve.RegularProlongation.disc_sections_locality_of_smoothPoint) together with the curve and principal-ideal-ring facts for the base-changed function field of $X_H$. It feeds the assembly of the ends and residue-disc cover in the node-layer step, [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.supersingularProlongation_ends_residueDiscs_cover_of_affineChart_poles_hasse_commonChart_nodes`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.supersingularProlongation_ends_residueDiscs_cover_of_affineChart_poles_hasse_commonChart_nodes).
